are for childhood malaria in Zambia</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>1491</fpage><lpage>1503</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11077952</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0277-9536(00)00049-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Salako</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Brieger</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Afolabi</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Umeh</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Agomo</surname><given-names>PU</given-names></name><name><surname>Asa</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Adeneye</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Nwankwo</surname><given-names>BO</given-names></name><name><surname>Akinlade</surname><given-names>CO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Treatment of childhood fevers and other illnesses in three rural Nigerian communities</article-title><source>J Trop Paed</source><year>2001</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>230</fpage><lpage>238</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/tropej/47.4.230</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jimmy</surname><given-names>EO</given-names></name><name><surname>Achelonu</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Orji</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Antimalarials dispensing pattern by patent medicine dealers in rural settlements in Nigeria</article-title><source>Public Health</source><year>2000</year><volume>114</volume><fpage>282</fpage><lpage>285</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10962592</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0033-3506(00)00346-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ajayi</surname><given-names>IO</given-names></name><name><surname>Falade</surname><given-names>CO</given-names></name><name><surname>Adeniyi</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name><name><surname>Bolaji</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of patent medicine sellers in home management of malaria</article-title><source>Int Quarterly of Community Health Education</source><year>2002</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>271</fpage><lpage>281</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2190/569A-XLPX-YF5C-H9HU</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brieger</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Osamor</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name><name><surname>Salami</surname><given-names>KK</given-names></name><name><surname>Oladepo</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Otusanya</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Interaction between patent medicine vendors and customers in urban and rural Nigeria</article-title><source>Health Policy Plan</source><year>2004</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>177</fpage><lpage>182</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15070866</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/heapol/czh021</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Okonkwo</surname><given-names>PO</given-names></name><name><surname>Akpala</surname><given-names>CO</given-names></name><name><surname>Okafor</surname><given-names>HU</given-names></name><name><surname>Mbah</surname><given-names>AU</given-names></name><name><surname>Nwaiwu</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Compliance to correct dose of chloroquine in uncomplicated malaria correlates with improvement in the condition of rural Nigerian children</article-title><source>Trans R Soc Trop Med Hyg</source><year>2001</year><volume>95</volume><fpage>320</fpage><lpage>324</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11491007</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0035-9203(01)90252-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pagnoni</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Convelbo</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Tiendrebeogo</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Cousens</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Esposito</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A community based programme to provide prompt and adequate treatment of presumptive malaria in children</article-title><source>Trans R Soc Trop Med Hyg</source><year>1997</year><volume>91</volume><fpage>512</fpage><lpage>517</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9463653</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0035-9203(97)90006-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marsh</surname><given-names>VM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mutemi</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name><name><surname>Muturi</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Haaland</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Watkins</surname><given-names>WM</given-names></name><name><surname>Otieno</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Marsh</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Changing home treatment of childhood fevers by training shop keepers in rural Kenya</article-title><source>Trop Med Int Health</source><year>1999</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>383</fpage><lpage>389</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10402975</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-3156.1999.00403.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kidane</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Morrow</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Teaching mothers to provide home treatment of malaria in Tigray, Ethiopia: a randomized trial</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2000</year><volume>356</volume><fpage>550</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10950232</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(00)02580-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Falade</surname><given-names>CO</given-names></name><name><surname>Ogundiran</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name><name><surname>Bolaji</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name><name><surname>Ajayi</surname><given-names>IO</given-names></name><name><surname>Akinboye</surname><given-names>DO</given-names></name><name><surname>Oladepo</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Adeniyi</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Oduola</surname><given-names>AMJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of cultural perception of causation, complications and severity of childhood malaria as determinants of treatment and preventive pathways</article-title><source>Int Quarterly of Community Health Education</source><year>2005</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>345</fpage><lpage>361</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>NPC</collab></person-group><article-title>Final result of 1991 population census of Nigeria</article-title><source>National Population Commission</source><year>1991</year></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fawole</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Onadeko</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Knowledge and home of malaria fever by mothers and caregivers for under-five children</article-title><source>West Afr J Med</source><year>2001</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>152</fpage><lpage>157</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11768016</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deming</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gayibor</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Murphy</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>TS</given-names></name><name><surname>Karsa</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The home treatment of febrile children with antimalaria drugs in Togo</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><year>1989</year><volume>67</volume><fpage>695</fpage><lpage>700</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2633884</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brieger</surname><given-names>WR</given-names></name><name><surname>Onyido</surname><given-names>AE</given-names></name><name><surname>Sexton</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Ezike</surname><given-names>VI</given-names></name><name><surname>Breman</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>Ekanem</surname><given-names>OJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Monitoring community response to malaria control using insecticide &#x02013; impregnated bed nets, curtains and residual spray at Nsukka, Nigeria</article-title><source>Health Education Research Theory &#x00026; Practice</source><year>1996</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>133</fpage><lpage>145</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Adera</surname><given-names>TD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Beliefs and traditional treatment of malaria in Kishe settlement area, South West Ethiopia</article-title><source>Ethiop Med J</source><year>2003</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>34</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12764998</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vundule</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Mharakurwa</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Knowledge, practices and perceptions about malaria in rural communities of Zimbabwe: relevance to malaria control</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><year>1996</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>55</fpage><lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8653816</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Munguti</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Community perceptions and treatment seeking for malaria in Baringo district, Kenya</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>1998</year><volume>40</volume><fpage>1271</fpage><lpage>1277</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hamel</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Odhacha</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Roberts</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Deming</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Malaria control in Bungoma District, Kenya: A survey of home treatment of children with fever, bednet use and attendance at antenatal clinics</article-title><source>Bull World Health Organ</source><year>2001</year><volume>79</volume><fpage>1014</fpage><lpage>1023</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11731808</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Adeneye</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Jegede</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Mafe</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Nwokocha</surname><given-names>EE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A pilot study to evaluate malaria control strategies in Ogun State, Nigeria</article-title><source>World Health &#x00026; Population;</source><year>2007</year><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>12</lpage></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>